From e45bc665ccd58172a80dc3ad44e573f931581c16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 03:00:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] The Inner Garden, Phase 2: the drops
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every release becomes an event in her garden, and the portal ships honest
until the owner sets the first drop: src/lib/portal/drops.ts is empty, so
/members/drops says "No drop is open right now. The next one will bloom
here." with New in the garden, and no clock counts to nothing.

- The drop manifest (owner-written, documented in place) and a pure
  dropPhase: sealed, moved, members, public, arriving and vault, in IST
  (+05:30). "Arriving" means its time has passed but none of its pieces is
  on the shop; a listed piece that sold out reads Sold out, so a drop that
  sells out never claims it has not opened. dropProblems checks every entry.
- The server's clock: one same-origin HEAD per visit reads the Date header
  (plus Age), falling back to the phone's; one timer per minute boundary,
  no animation loop.
- The Bloom Clock: a sealed bud on a dotted gold dial whose five petals open
  at 7 days, 3 days, 1 day, 1 hour and the opening; "Opens Sat 21 Nov ·
  8:00 pm IST"; digits that roll in only as a minute passes, and the same
  time in words for a screen reader. A moved date is struck through.
  "Add to my calendar": Google Calendar first, then a .ics with a 30 minute
  reminder (not offered inside Instagram or Facebook's browser).
- The next drop's sealed bud stands in her garden's back row, growing in
  with it; her garden card tells of the next or open drop.
- A drop's room: rub the petals (a canvas of the drop's own petals, 28 px
  destination-out brush, DPR capped at 2, a 64 x 64 coverage mask read every
  8th move, the rest falling away at 55%) or Reveal, the same end state; no
  canvas under reduced motion. The unboxing, once per drop on a device: the
  Naira box (the portal's own CSS copy, so no shop chunk changes) turns,
  its drawer slides out, the lead piece rises, a glint crosses it and up to
  24 petals in the drop's colour fly on worked-out arcs, gone by 1.6 s;
  then the pieces unfold 60 ms apart. The pieces: live price and
  compare-at, Available or Sold out, her month already chosen, Add to bag
  and Buy now through the shop's bag, "Arriving · ask on WhatsApp" for a
  piece not on the shop yet. Press your flower: it turns a quarter and
  squashes flat into a gold herbarium frame, "Drop 01 · Verdant · pressed
  21 Nov", kept on this device and planted in her garden.
- New in the garden: the portal's own small Storefront query for
  publishedAt (the shop's catalogue query is untouched), the last 14 days
  as fresh shoots dated as they arrived.
- The Vault: every drop that has bloomed as a pressed-flower wall; one she
  did not press is a gentle empty frame, "This one bloomed in October".
- A Drops tab on the garden path; the gate now promises the first look and
  the pressed flower, and names the next drop only if the owner allows it.

Each room is its own lazy chunk with its own stylesheet (gzip -9): Drops
3.5 KB JS + 0.9 KB CSS, DropRoom 9.8 KB + 1.5 KB, Vault 1.1 KB + 0.4 KB,
sharing a calendar chunk (2.5 KB + 0.7 KB) and a frame chunk (0.5 KB +
0.6 KB). The route stays 25.9 KB JS and 3.6 KB CSS. The global stylesheet
and vendor chunk build byte-identical to origin/main, and every shop chunk
is unchanged but for the entry's hashed name. Development-only preview drops
(&drop=sealed|moved|members|public|arriving|vault on the preview member)
use real published pieces and are absent from the build.

Tests: dropPhase, clock, ics, newIn, the manifest, the Bloom Clock, the rub,
the drop rooms (empty manifest, once-per-device unboxing, petal cap, live
prices, layers), and copy and isolation rules for the new rooms.

